/strong></p>',1,'<p>awesome</p>','<p>freezing</p>','<p>starving</p>','<p>exhausted</p>','','D','','','','','','',''),(21,1,21,'<p class=\"Default\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Creole Onion Soup</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">This is a traditional French dish adapted by the Creoles of New Orleans. It is sometimes known as Looney soup</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Ingredients</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">75 gr unsalted</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">6 large onions, peeled and sliced</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Salt and pepper</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">1 tbsp brown sugar</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">600 ml beef stock</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">60 gr plain flour</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">2 tsp soy sauce</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">1 tsp Worcester sauce</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">6 slices of French bread</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">6 tbsp grated cheese</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Method</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(1) Melt butter slowly</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(2) Add sliced onion, a pinch of a salt and pepper and the sugar.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(3) Cook on a slow heat, stirring from time to time, until the onions have browned.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(4) Add veg stock and bring to the boil</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(5) sift the flour, stirring hard to avoid lumps</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(6) Add chicken stock</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(7) Simmer for 3-4 hours</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(8) Add sauces</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(9) Top each bowl with bread and cheese. It should be served for 4 to 6 people.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">How much Worcester sauce do you need to make creoles onion soup?</span></p>',1,'<p>One tsp</p>','<p>One tbsp</p>','<p>Two tsp</p>','<p>Six tbsp</p>','','A','','','','','','',''),(22,1,22,'<p class=\"Default\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Creole Onion Soup</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">This is a traditional French dish adapted by the Creoles of New Orleans. It is sometimes known as Looney soup</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Ingredients</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">75 gr unsalted</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">6 large onions, peeled and sliced</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Salt and pepper</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">1 tbsp brown sugar</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">600 ml beef stock</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">60 gr plain flour</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">2 tsp soy sauce</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">1 tsp Worcester sauce</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">6 slices of French bread</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">6 tbsp grated cheese</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Method</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(1) Melt butter slowly</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(2) Add sliced onion, a pinch of a salt and pepper and the sugar.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(3) Cook on a slow heat, stirring from time to time, until the onions have browned.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(4) Add veg stock and bring to the boil</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(5) sift the flour, stirring hard to avoid lumps</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(6) Add chicken stock</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(7) Simmer for 3-4 hours</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(8) Add sauces</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">(9) Top each bowl with bread and cheese. It should be served for 4 to 6 people.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Why should you warn your guest while having the soup?</span></p>',1,'<p>You won&rsquo;t want much else to eat</p>','<p>The bowl is placed under grill.</p>','<p>The cheese has melted</p>','<p>The bowls are hot</p>','','C','','','','','','',''),(23,1,23,'<p class=\"Default\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Creole Onion Soup</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">This is a traditional French dish adapted by the Creoles of New Orleans. It is sometimes known as Looney soup</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Ingredients</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">75 gr unsalted</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">6 large onions, peeled and sliced</span><